## RESOLVED 2026-08-24 - Whole-container ECC framing (format v3)
Implemented in Wave K: RS(255,191) coded control header carrying all
self-describing fields + RS-coded body covering metadata + payload + CRC.
v2 containers fail closed. See container-wire-format.md section 3.

## REJECTED 2026-08-24 - Signed manifest verification layer (Ed25519)
REJECTED on post-quantum grounds. Ed25519 relies on elliptic-curve discrete
logarithm, which Shor's algorithm breaks completely. The existing HMAC-SHA256
manifest authentication is already post-quantum resistant (symmetric primitive,
Grover's algorithm provides only quadratic speedup). Adding Ed25519 would have
introduced the sole quantum-vulnerable component into an otherwise PQ-safe
system. The design goal is purely symmetric cryptography throughout.

## 2026-08-23 - Full fuzzing + metamorphic testing coverage (all layers)

Goal: every module owned by seeded, structure-aware fuzzing plus explicit
metamorphic relations (MRs), not just example tests. Builds on the seeded
pbt.js harness and the Wave H fuzz/MR culture (npm run fuzz; CI smoke slice).
Track per-layer adoption; "done" = listed MRs/generators exist + long-run
fuzz script exercises them without finding open counterexamples.

Current: wire-format L0-L3 (conformance + 12 PBT), capacity scanner,
escapeHtml, vault structures, algebraic transforms, huffman encoder.

- [x] codec: encode/decode roundtrip fuzzing (random dimensions/quality/
      subsampling/restart intervals); MRs - decode-after-encode stability,
      quality-vs-size monotonicity, dimension preservation
- [x] automata parsers (marker-scanner, dht/dqt/sof/sos/spiff): mutated-JPEG
      generator (truncation, marker injection, lying length fields); MR -
      valid files unchanged, hostile input always fails closed
- [x] bit-streams: differential testing across BitReader variants on random
      streams (all three must agree bit-for-bit)
- [x] error-correction core: GF(256) field axioms as properties; RS
      roundtrip under random corruption distributions at tolerance edges;
      interleave permutation-invariance MRs
- [x] cryptography: AES-GCM/PBKDF2/HMAC roundtrip + AAD-binding properties
      (structural; CSPRNG prevents byte vectors)
- [x] vault layer: operation-sequence fuzzing against invariants (locked
      never decrypts, revision strictly increases, freeze holds); MR -
      clone chains equivalent to batch operations
- [x] batch embedder/extractor: carrier-subset selection MRs, allocation
      determinism, capacity-bound enforcement
- [x] scripts/cli.mjs: argument fuzzing, fail-closed exit codes
- [x] harness: npm run fuzz driver landed (CI smoke + scalable local runs); full corpus
Related: RESOLVED whole-container ECC framing entry (see top of file).

